[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known: "one issue, one fix queued".
The reports in it describe three different problems. The queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one bug. Each problem below has its own ticket now. Do not close the other two when the parser fix ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## Why the merge hid them

- **Merged on subject.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose
  subjects match, and nobody reads the body. "Wrong date" fits all three problems.
- **The cause depends on the tenant, not the browser.** Intake tags each report from the reporter's
  browser. Whether a report is `parser` or `hint` depends on the tenant's locale and booking form.
  Intake and the tenant disagree on many of these reports.
- **A report that is not a swap still counted as one.** The desk read some reports as a one-day move,
  then filed them under `parser` by tenant. They have their own cause.
- **The export repeats rows.** The ticket export has overlapping pages. Count each report id once.

## The #4471 view, for comparison

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

- Ship the parser fix and close the `parser` ticket only.
- Fix the booking-v3 date hint separately. The parser fix does not touch it.
- Look for a time-zone or day-boundary bug for the one-day reports.
- Match duplicates on cause (tenant and way in), not on subject.

